From: John Audia <therealgraysky@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:00:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] kernel: bump 6.18 to 6.18.62

Changelog: https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v6.x/ChangeLog-6.18.61*
Changelog: https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v6.x/ChangeLog-6.18.62

Removed upstreamed:
  linux/generic/backport-6.18/503-01-v7.3-ksmbd-enable-tcp-keepalive-for-accepted-connections.patch[1]
  linux/generic/backport-6.18/734-v7.3-net-ethernet-mtk_wed-increase-WED-v2-WDMA-RESV_BUFF-.patch[2]
  linux/generic/backport-6.18/856-01-v7.3-xhci-include-all-root-port-children-in-recovery-prevention-on-link-error.patch[3]
  linux/generic/backport-6.18/755-v7.3-net-sfp-add-quirk-for-HORACO-copper-SFP-module.patch[4]

Manually rebased:
  linux/generic/backport-6.18/441-v7.4-spi-spi-qpic-snand-publish-the-ECC-context-to-snandc.patch
  linux/generic/pending-6.18/739-03-net-pcs-pcs-mtk-lynxi-add-platform-driver-for-MT7988.patch
  linux/bcm27xx/patches-6.18/0120-hid-usb-Add-device-quirks-for-Freeway-Airmouse-T3-an.patch
  linux/bcm27xx/patches-6.18/0940-dma-dw-axi-dmac-fix-cyclic-DMA.patch

All other patches automatically rebased via update_kernel.sh

mac80211: 6.18.62 reverts the sockaddr_unsized conversion[5], so drop
160-backports-sockaddr_unsized-is-in-6.18.57.patch.

ltq-ifxos: guard the sockaddr_unsized bind() cast on 6.19 instead of
6.18.57 for the same reason.

* Skipped, 6.18.62 avoided distributing a kernel with known security flaws
  only to replace .61 almost immediately. CVE-2026-100080
  CVE-2026-100081 CVE-2026-100082.

1. https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/stable/linux.git/commit/?h=v6.18.62&id=b78a4334a8927d4dcc692382a45b420109bcb071
2. https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/stable/linux.git/commit/?h=v6.18.62&id=855236abde29727de86a39fa7b2371098f166f6b
3. https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/stable/linux.git/commit/?h=v6.18.62&id=89e76d0fc8d25a47c391b56d5c34367759612c8e
